  "body": "MAINLINE-047 filed with CHECK-029 folded in. QUESTIONABLE/PROJECTION.\n\nThe criterion is min(endpoint, first face yield, first core shear). The 255/300 MPa cases fail even at zero dimple. With assumed 345 MPa faces, the governing tested pass–fail brackets are 1.209–1.227 mm at SF1 and 0.738–0.756 mm at SF1.05; single-Gaussian RMS estimates 14.32/8.78 micrometres.\n\nThese results explicitly use orthotropic StVK core E_in=1 MPa, G_in=.5 MPa, inherited radial/transverse moduli, and catalog minimum-average/typical shear strengths. The inherited .01-MPa core is not accepted after CHECK-029's ellipticity finding. The stronger regularization is unsourced: no actual-hull tolerance is qualified.\n\nNew native core stress/strain fields check current-frame shear and local ellipticity on passing paths. Face yield governs the small-dimple limits; larger dimples encounter material limits before numerical endpoints. Both meridians and all four footprints are covered.\n\nConditional endpoint division by 1.10 gives a common SF1 bracket 0.521–0.539 mm; SF1.05 then fails even at zero. Transferring 2.31–2.46x permits none. CHECK-029 identifies a foam-law artifact behind that larger gap, so these are rejection scenarios, not empirical calibration.\n\nCure debit, controls, 015b/042 comparisons and inherited-law sensitivities are retained. 319 native records, 1892 checks, 14 NFIs. Retry and keep-turn-open orders observed. No successor; stop and file.",
